(project pricklypear-filmstrip
 (doc "Pricklypear book chapter: FILMSTRIP — the habitat shell. Two infinite horizontal strips stacked iTunes-style: the top strip is a Miller-column cascade (structural menus, not popups), the bottom strip is the niri-style row of content panes. Panes are ordinary routes in partial mode — they don't know they're windowed. Workspace state is a per-user row; the desktop persists in the same object store as the todos it displays.")
 (status implemented)
 (* agent note (|2026-09 DESIGN SESSION (with pads.borg): the user's sketch (waybar + three small top panels + one large content area, \"kind of how iTunes is laid out\") plus \"two separate infinite horizontal panes\" crystallized the model. Prior art named in-session: iTunes column browser / Finder column view / ranger / Smalltalk browser for the top (Miller-column cascade); niri (and not-quite acme) for the bottom. The point that made it click: the cascade is STATE, not styling — which is why the filmstrip idea never modalized in CSS. Filmstrip is the FIRST consumer of pads vocabulary but is itself buildable stringly as a product; pads migration makes it provable. Dialog/overlay needs come from pads/layers-modality; filmstrip keeps floats for genuinely transient things only — navigation is structural.|) *)
 (* agent note (|2026-09-04 MAKE (filmstrip v1, branch filmstrip-v1): shell shipped stringly per the handoff plan (docs/plans/filmstrip-v1.md). Dialect notes for the next agent: let* is a SINGLE-BODY macro — multi-step handlers wrap their tail in (seq ...); cons builds VPair chains which count rejects (length accepts both). browse lives as <pkg>/browse defs inside libs/filmstrip until promotion into todo/notes/calendar. Routes are exact-match, so /filmstrip/width/<id> became /filmstrip/<action> routes with id/dir/d/t params — same semantics, different spelling than this chapter's prose. Smoke: scripts/smoke_filmstrip.py (11 checks incl. zero-JS + round-trip).|) *)
 (convention ocaml-dune)

 (section filmstrip-shell
  (doc "The default habitat view. Screen model: a column of two rows —
      the cascade strip (short, iTunes browser proportions) over the
      content strip (grow). Both scroll horizontally and independently;
      both are ordinary pad rows with (scroll . x) once pads exists.
      Panes do not know they are windowed: a pane is any route
      dispatched in partial mode (HX-Request on — the route gate's
      existing fragment path, the hyper/visit trick productized). All
      htmx inside a pane works unchanged, targeting its own fragment.")

  (subsection workspace-model
   (doc "Per-user workspace row: two sequences plus focus. cascade = an
       ordered crumb path; content = an ordered list of pane records
       {id route width}; focus = (strip . index). Open/close/focus/
       width-preset are row mutations rendered back as swaps — the
       strip follows niri's set-column-width presets (third / half /
       full), never free pixel widths. Sessions persist: close the
       laptop, the strip is where you left it, because the row is
       Postgres like everything else grown in the garden.")
   (details
    (doc (|
         ROW SHAPE (target):
           (ws (user)
             (cascade (list \"packages\" \"todo\" \"today\"))
             (content (list (pane todo/today 'half)
                            (pane notes/inbox 'third)))
             (focus (cons 'content 0)))
         EPHEMERAL CORNER (pads/layers-modality rule applied): scroll
         position, hovered pane, live-drag in progress — transient,
         keyed by pane id, patched around on sync; never rendered from.
    |))
   )
   (implements libs/filmstrip/lib.pp scripts/smoke_filmstrip.py)
   (status implemented)
  )

  (subsection cascade-protocol
   (doc "The top strip is a Miller-column cascade: column N's selection
       determines column N+1; the deepest selection acts on the content
       strip. One function per package makes it filmstrip-native:
       (pkg/browse path) -> (columns . leaf?). Clicking an entry at
       depth d truncates the path to d, appends the choice, swaps the
       tail columns. Leaf action opens-or-focuses a content pane.
       Menus as STRUCTURE, not popups — plan 9's menus-are-text moved
       from overlay into chrome; the float band survives only for
       genuinely transient things (confirmations, plumbing menus,
       notifications).")
   (details
    (doc (|
         BROWSE IS THE WHOLE TRICK. Every package already has the
         shape, it just renders it wrong today:
           notes     outline headings walk down
           calendar  year -> month -> day
           bible     book -> chapter -> verse (dabar/strongs adjacent)
           contacts  group -> person
           todo      list -> item
         DECISION RECORDED: cascade is GLOBAL v1 — one crumb path for
         the shell, iTunes-style. Per-pane cascades (each content pane
         carrying its own crumb path, workspace = N uniform cascade+
         content columns) is the elegant unification but doubles the
         state surface; revisit after v1 is dogfooded. NOTIFICATIONS:
         transient cards in the cascade strip (waybar's \"pi finished\"
         earns a home), promotable into content panes or dismissed —
         filmstrip gives notifications a place to LIVE that isn't a
         popup.
    |))
   )
   (status implemented)
  )

  (subsection pane-protocol
   (doc "A pane = route dispatched in-process with HX-Request on, the
       route gate's existing fragment path. Zero-JS hotkeys: htmx key
       filters on the shell body (keydown[altKey&&key=='ArrowLeft'] and
       kin) POST focus/width/open to filmstrip routes; the server owns
       which pane wears .focused and answers with OOB class swaps.
       Optional JS is quarantined to ONE static file and buys only
       scroll-into-view smoothness and horizontal wheel mapping —
       nothing semantic. Twin-pane mode is a first-class pane kind for
       the pads migration: one column showing [old string render |
       pads-lowered render | soup/diff badge] — drift as something you
       LOOK at, pads/drift-proofing made interactive.")
   (details
    (doc (|
         NO NEW SUBSTRATE inventory (why this is a product, not a
         research project): route/lookup + route/dispatch with the
         header seam already exist; the route gate already serves
         partial mode; css/sheet + theme/ extend to ~50 lines of strip
         CSS; the workspace row is data_rows; the only optional
         non-Nopales artifact is the quarantined scroll.js. Nothing in
         image/ moves for v1.
    |))
   )
   (status implemented)
  )

  (subsection shell-events
   (doc "Open: launcher picks a route, POST /filmstrip/open, server
       appends the pane record and dispatches the route — fragment goes
       beforeend into the strip. Close/width/focus likewise: row
       mutation, then minimal OOB swaps (this is the ops-contract of
       pads worn by the web backend before pads exists — the shell is
       the ops pilot). Dialogs and menus follow pads/layers-modality:
       a #layers sibling of the strips takes float/scrim nodes; modal
       = router scope while the node lives.")
   (verify
    (smoke "open todo -> strip gains pane with todo partial; interactions inside pane swap in-place")
    (smoke "alt+arrows move .focused between panes with no JS")
    (smoke "workspace row round-trip: reload restores strip order/widths/focus")
    (smoke "cascade: packages -> todo -> today opens the today pane; truncation re-walks"))
   (status implemented)
  )

  (subsection window-controlbox-v2
   (doc "V2 shell model (glochid-led, habitat-shared). Two primitives, following acme: WINDOW = tag + body (tag row of words over a dispatched route fragment; the filmstrip pane head already IS a tag), CONTROLBOX = one labeled row of words where each word is a mutation POST (rail rows, pane heads, shelf rows are all control boxes). Everything renders from DECLARED STATE, never estimate geometry in code: panes gain region (rail | main), desktop (int), state (live | shelved); the workspace row grows a desktop int. The shell is two scroll-strips — a RAIL strip (vertical on wide-short screens, top-rotatable by 3 CSS rules; modes are rail panes: apps/files/windows/shelf, for PICKING not reading) over a MAIN strip (the niri horizontal strip third/half/full, unconditional) — same mutations on both. VIRTUAL DESKTOPS are class flips: one sentinel carries the current desktop, a generated :has() set display:nones the rest; zero JS. Shelf is the DEFAULT close (DOM survives via hx-preserve; shelf rows carry destroy; destroy is the OOB delete that exists today). NAV DISCIPLINE is part of the vocabulary: app-link = open-or-focus POST for cross-app nav; pane-local links target closest .fs-body; plain <a> is shell-level only (a pane escaping the shell — plain <a> inside a fragment — is a BUG CLASS, fixed by app-link). Focus always heals so a focused main pane exists while panes do. make harness: seeded fake workspace on a scratch instance, CDP screenshots with measured geometry per mutation; live hosts touched last.")
   (* agent note (|2026-09-13 DESIGN SESSION (glochid rail work): the col axis grew the left rail (shell narrows to ~20rem; cascade stacks as a vertical app menu; presets re-read as rail heights — landed), then the focused pane was LIFTED into the main window via position:fixed with rail rows heads-only (landed; .chatpage height:100% fix landed with it). Session then RENAMED the target: main = niri strip (option B, not master-stack), sidebar = own scroll strip, desktops like hyprland via CSS hiding, close defaults to shelf, no JS drag — never. Inspiration named: acme tag lines = control boxes; gui-better-than-tui via TWO simple primitives instead of a renderer. Hidden-DOM cost confirmed negligible; live-updating shelved DOM is the only budget (later: server pauses streams to shelved panes). What landed pre-v2 stays in agent.borg filmstrip-shell; THIS stanza owns the forward model.|) *)
   (* agent note (|2026-09-14 UI REVIEW CYCLE CLOSED (dogfood + agent review, docs/reviews/glochid-shell-review-2026-09-14.md): the review CONFIRMED this stanza's model but caught three behavior gaps the geometry probes PASSED — (a) open-or-focus didn't know state: clicking a shelved app's cascade name moved .focused onto a display:none pane and BLANKED the main window; FIXED acme-get style (naming a hidden window re-shows it — open-apply unshelves on route hit) in 22906c9; (b) open/cascade mutations never refreshed the windows rail, so #fs-winbox went stale; FIXED same commit (shelf/winbox OOB hooks now answered on every open win); (c) the plain-<a> bug class was still live on every fragment surface (/code rows, chat h1 'agent' + resumed line, sessions resume/view, settings h1) — /code rows are pane-local links now (hx-target closest .fs-body, the tree walk stays INSIDE the pane), redirect-actions got fragment twins (POST /filmstrip/new, /filmstrip/resume; 2db1008), settings fragment h1 de-anchored (9a7bd3b via probe I5). The launcher advertised /todos on glochid (host vocab leak): placeholder + no-route message now derive from filmstrip/ hints themselves (hint-routes over the host's apps — glochid ALSO redefines filmstrip/apps now, which the host-variation note already named as allowed). The open-apply no-desktop gap (REPORT of docs/plans/window-controlbox-v2.md) is CLOSED via the filmstrip/pane-stamp host hook: fresh panes stamp the operator's current desktop. NEW HARNESS: scripts/probe_shell_sem.mjs asserts the invariants semantically (I1 visible-focused-always · I2 shelved-click unshelves · I3 winbox freshness · I4 launcher honesty · I5 pane-local anchors · I6 in-pane tree walk · I7 current-desktop stamp) — ALL GREEN, lisp/common runtest green, chat smoke green.|) *)
   (implements scripts/probe_shell_wm.mjs scripts/probe_shell_sem.mjs)
   (verify
    (smoke "desktop flip: sentinel class change toggles which panes render; others display:none but keep live DOM")
    (smoke "shelve: close moves pane to the shelf rail pane with DOM intact; restore returns it to its desktop+position")
    (smoke "app-link inside a pane open-or-focuses the target route; a plain <a> inside a fragment never escapes the shell")
    (smoke "geometry probe: seeded 8-pane 3-desktop workspace renders from state classes only (no inline styles)")
    (smoke "semantic probe (scripts/probe_shell_sem.mjs): I1 visible-focused-always · I2 shelved-click unshelves (no 0x0 focused pane) · I3 winbox freshness · I4 launcher names only real host routes · I5 every fragment anchor pane-local · I6 /code dir walk inside the pane · I7 fresh panes stamp the current desktop — ALL GREEN")
    (smoke "open-or-focus on a shelved route UNSHELVES it (acme Get); launcher placeholder + no-route message list only routes the host has"))
   (status implemented)
  )

  (subsection window-controlbox-v3
   (doc "V3 shell model: REGION SHIPS. window-controlbox-v2 declared panes gain region (rail | main) — the implementation never read it, so the rail is heads-only and exactly ONE body is ever on stage; the operator cannot hold two reading views at once (file tree + chat — the 2026-09-14 review's biggest ask + its design findings 1-3: dead rail middle, 16rem-capped cascade that cannot grow into the space it owns). V3 implements region as a pane-head PIN verb. region=rail panes render their LIVE BODY inside the rail (between the cascade and the controlboxes — filling the dead middle); region=main panes keep the v2 model (strip + one lifted focused pane, unchanged). RAIL PANES ARE DESKTOP-GLOBAL (dock semantics: one sidebar visible across desktop flips — no per-desktop duplication of a file tree). At most one lifted main pane exists at a time; focusing a rail pane highlights it WITHOUT lifting; open-or-focus of a pinned route highlights the rail pane in place instead of stealing the main window (and must never heal-focus onto a shelved pane — the I2 invariant holds in both regions). The FILE TREE graduates from a cascade walk to a pinned /code pane: the cascade keeps only PICKING (column 0 apps), the rail pane is the READING view at full rail height. Pane records carry region; all geometry stays in glochid/base-css as classes + :has — zero JS, zero inline styles, same discipline as v2. Make harness: scratch instance + CDP with scripts/probe_shell_sem.mjs (batch B) as the GATE — semantic invariants first, geometry second; live hosts last.")
   (verify
    (smoke "pin /code -> its body renders in the rail at a real height while /chat stays lifted in the main window; zero inline styles introduced")
    (smoke "rail pin survives desktop flips (dock semantics); unpin returns the pane to the strip at its old position")
    (smoke "open-or-focus on a pinned route highlights the rail pane in place (no lift, no 0x0 focused pane, I1/I2 hold)")
    (smoke "probe_shell_sem.mjs ALL GREEN after every mutation (invariants are the gate; extend it with region invariants)")
    (smoke "shelving a rail-region pane shelves it like any pane (shelf row; restore restores region)")
    (smoke "a pinned files view fills available rail height — the cascade 16rem cap no longer bounds it")
    (smoke "workspace round-trip: region persists through save-all and reload")
   )
   (status planned)
  )

  (subsection roadmap-tiers
   (doc "Where filmstrip points once the web product runs: (1) pads
       migration makes the shell a pad tree — the same workspace value
       then lowers to pads/render-ansi for a terminal desktop beside
       pp-eval, and the twin-pane verify loop runs the port route by
       route. (2) The native tier (river-protocol shim, C/clay soil)
       consumes the SAME two-sequence workspace: policy events are
       Lisp-frequency; frames never eval (pads/renderer-dialects
       latency non-goal). (3) Multi-user + one seat stays the known
       weirdness: single seat resolves to admin's workspace row; per-
       identity strips are a later flourish, not a v1 promise.")
 (* agent note (|2026-09-04 (soil M-A): roadmap tier (1) has STARTED — filmstrip/scene (in libs/filmstrip/lib.pp) renders the workspace as a pad tree via pads/render-scene; the native kiosk (soil-hello --eval "(filmstrip/scene)") consumes it (scripts/smoke_soil_ma.py). The HTML shell is unchanged; scene + HTML are two lowerings of one workspace row. Terminal (render-ansi) remains open.|) *)
 (* agent note (|2026-09-04 PROMOTE: filmstrip + pads promoted to system/main on the dev stack AND on prod (pricklypear.rocks) — /filmstrip live for all identities, scene verified on prod; master merged (filmstrip-v1 fast-forward). Debt noted: todo/notes/calendar browse defs still live inside libs/filmstrip (one-file make constraint); promotion into their home packages is the next hygiene pass.|) *)
 (* agent note (|2026-09-11 HOST VARIATION (glochid shell, see agent.borg filmstrip-shell): the filmstrip lib now boots on the AGENT host too, as glochid's surface — the harness's request-runner seam makes this a load, not a port. Two seams are intentionally HOST-PROVIDED and this note records the allowed variation: (1) WORKSPACE BACKING — filmstrip/ws-node / ws-save are the persistence seam; the habitat uses tree/get + tree/upsert (one-tree, per-identity row), glochid redefines them over fs prims into .agent/workspace.json. Per-workspace state on a laptop is local-first state, NOT habitat content — retaining tree backing as the image default is right; a lens-backed row (same workspace following the operator across devices) is the deferred unification. (2) THE CASCADE INVENTORY — filmstrip/browse / pkg-browse / filmstrip/apps are the app list; the habitat lists todo/notes/calendar, glochid lists its own surfaces (chat/code/sessions/settings/memory with a filesystem cascade for code). Everything else (strips, OOB swap grammar, zero-JS keys, open-or-focus, width presets) is the LIB's and stays shared. status here stays; glochid's stanza lives in agent.borg.|) *)
   (status planned)
  )
 )
)
